 and nothing else (no prose, no markdown fences):\n{\"edits\":[{\"name\":\"KC\",\"value\":128}],\"rationale\":\"one or two sentences\"}\nFacts and strategy:\n- The BASELINE values above are the hand-tuned defaults and are a strong starting point; the kernel is HBM-bandwidth bound.\n- Dev launches route only 2..32 tokens in total (Tv+Td), top-8 of 128 experts, so most experts see only a few tokens (uniform expectation = 8*T/128 pairs per expert). The 2-row-tile path (pair_cnt > MT_SPLIT) doubles accumulator registers and MMA work on padded rows for the SAME weight traffic; lowering MT_SPLIT moves more experts onto it. Raising MT_SPLIT back to 16 is the maximum.\n- smem rows are read by 16x16 WMMA loads in 16-byte chunks. A row stride (in bytes) that is an ODD multiple of 16 spreads 8 rows over all 8 bank groups (conflict free); stride = 128B*k + 16B*odd works, e.g. pad 8 or 24 or 40. Pad 0 gives 8-way conflicts and pad 16 gives 2-way conflicts.\n- KC trades smem footprint and sync count: smaller KC means more __syncthreads rounds and shorter weight-load bursts; larger KC means more smem.\n- Earlier proposals this session list their measured dev speedup. Do NOT repeat a combination that measured < 1.0; change at most 1-2 tunables per proposal so the effect is attributable, and move AWAY from directions that already measured slower. The speed gate needs a dev speedup above the stated threshold, so an empty edit list is better than a guess you expect to be slower.\nRules: at most 5 edits; each name at most once; values are integers (no strings, no expressions); no other keys. Do NOT write a diff; the harness renders it. If you see no safe improvement output {\"edits\":[],\"rationale\":\"...\"}.", "prompt_sha256": "ad8ff9cfd898d0bc787f2d2d04929c5043a73f4185ea830927c38625685b748c", "raw_response": "{\"edits\":[{\"name\":\"KC\",\"value\":128}],\"rationale\":\"MOCK\"}", "raw_response_sha256": "6f0321afebbf0774ba4a2a091472b4e0a9025968363535cae3357ff98f50ee23", "diff": "--- a